sentence:
These responsibilities include the design, implementation, operation and maintenance of adequate internal financial controls 
that if operating effectively would ensure the orderly and efficient conduct of its business, including:
-	
adherence to Group’s policies;
-	
the safeguarding of its assets;
-	
the prevention and detection of frauds and errors;
-	
the accuracy and completeness of the accounting records;
-	
the timely preparation of reliable financial information; and 
-	
compliance with applicable laws and regulations, including the QFMA’s law and relevant legislations and the Governance Code 
for Companies & Legal Entities Listed on the Main Market issued by the QFMA’s Board pursuant to Decision No. (
